    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0481" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6067</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-31T18:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.55 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister of Marine assured me that if Germany’s reply to Argentine demands is not
                    unconditional acceptance, Argentina will declare war. If Germany accepts, laws
                    of Argentina will be suspended in order to facilitate registration of vessels
                    under Argentine flag.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
